# Trivy exception list
#
# Enforcement blocks on HIGH and CRITICAL findings that have a fix available
# (every scan runs with --ignore-unfixed). This file is the pressure valve for
# findings that are genuinely accepted -- not a dumping ground for noise.
#
# Every entry MUST carry, on the lines above it:
#   - who accepted it
#   - why it is not exploitable here, or what compensating control applies
#   - an expiry date (review at the next release; delete the entry when it passes)
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#
# Example:
#   # Accepted by @platform-security 2026-08-24
#   # Reachable only via the CLI parser, which this service never invokes.
#   # Re-evaluate when the base image is bumped.
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-11-30
#
# An empty file means nothing is currently excepted. Keep it that way where possible.
